// One continent per country in lib/countries.ts's COUNTRIES list, using the
// standard 6-populated-continent model (Antarctica has no entries there).
// A handful of countries straddle two continents by strict geography —
// Russia, Turkey, Georgia, Armenia, Azerbaijan, Kazakhstan, Cyprus — each
// assigned to whichever side the UN geoscheme (or, for Cyprus, EU
// membership) puts it under, not a personal judgment call. Scotland/Wales/
// England (tracked as their own "countries" for travel purposes, see
// lib/countries.ts) all fall under Europe alongside the United Kingdom.
